        "fun": "The Pokémon world's lucky cat: the gold koban coin on Meowth's forehead comes from Japan's beckoning maneki-neko. It can't resist anything round and shiny, and prowls city streets at night picking up dropped change. Meowth is the only Pokémon with regional forms from two different regions, and the only one with both a regional form and a Gigantamax form.",
        "guide": "A nocturnal cat Pokémon modelled on Japan's maneki-neko, with a gold koban coin set in its forehead. Meowth is drawn to round, shiny objects and picks up loose change on city streets at night. It has regional forms in both Alola and Galar.",
        "tagline": "The lucky cat that can't walk past a shiny coin.",
